{"id":"neon-ooze","title":"Neon Ooze","url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Neon_Ooze","rev":237228,"fetched":"2026-10-16","lead":[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"b","c":["Neon Ooze"]}," is an aesthetic that developed in the 80s and 90s and was used most commonly for targeting children through gross-out marketing. The driving visual element were fluids such as slime, goop or toxic waste, with other related elements often thrown in such as nuclear, mad science or \"creepy crawly\" imagery. It reflects an era's playful obsession with eco-anxiety and gross-out humor."]}],"sections":[{"title":"History","id":"history","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["Neon Ooze originated in the late 1980s, partly from real-world worries about toxic waste disposal and pollution of the time."]}]},{"title":"Visuals","id":"visuals","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["Neon Ooze is defined by zany and kitschy gross-out imagery. Green and purple are the colors most associated with the aesthetic. Fluids are a key visual as many photo subjects would be covered in slime, goop or toxic waste."]}]},{"title":"Media","id":"media","blocks":[{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Video Games"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["The Ooze (1995)"]},{"c":["Boogerman: A Plick and Flick Adventure (1994)"]}]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Toys"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["ToyMax Creepy Crawlers workshop (1992)"]},{"c":["Trash Pack (2011-2014)"]}]}]},{"title":"Gallery","id":"gallery","blocks":[{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/7/71/IMG_6460.jpeg/revision/latest?cb=20240111052337","w":160,"h":221},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/6/6b/Earthbound.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20251219045416","w":160,"h":205},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/a/a7/The_stuff.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20251219045520","w":160,"h":213},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/6/68/Captain_planet.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20251219045157","w":161,"h":120},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocoo